From b3faabe9478175ff01550c5e586b64216ec4edfa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Code Review <claude-review@example.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 21:45:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add email verification and Cloudflare Turnstile bot
 protection
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Email verification:
- User gets verifyTokenHash/verifyTokenExpires (hashed, 24h, single-use,
  same approach as password reset); migration included. The existing
  emailVerified column is finally used.
- register sends a verification email (best effort — a failed send
  doesn't undo the signup; Sentry is notified)
- /verify-email page + POST /api/auth/verify-email consume the token
- POST /api/auth/resend-verification (signed in, 3/hour) for lost
  emails; dashboard shows a banner with a resend button until verified
- changing your email in Settings resets verified status and sends a
  link to the NEW address; re-saving the same email does not
- emailVerified is carried in the JWT/session, refreshed on update()
- Not enforced: unverified users can still create links. Gating link
  creation on verification is a one-line check in qr/create if wanted.

Bot protection:
- Cloudflare Turnstile on the register form (TurnstileWidget, explicit
  rendering so it works when toggling between sign in / register)
- server verifies the token before any database work, after cheap
  input validation so a typo doesn't burn the single-use token
- skipped when TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY / site key aren't set; once set it
  fails closed (missing, rejected, unreachable, or >5s all reject)

Privacy policy now lists Resend, Upstash, Sentry, and Cloudflare
Turnstile and what each receives.

Depends on the landing-page patch (login.js, restyled dashboard) and
the Upstash/Sentry patch (createLimiter, Sentry).
